<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Annales Cambriae</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Welsh Annals</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Annales Cambriae, or Welsh Annals, are a set of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> chronicles compiled in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>, the oldest version probably at St <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">Davids</a> in the 10th century. They record events from the mid-5th century onwards, including the battles of Badon and Camlann, the deaths of kings and the attacks of Mercians and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Vikings</a>. They are a basic source for early medieval Wales, though their earliest entries are of uncertain value.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/annales-cambriae.jpg" alt="Annales Cambriae" width="320" height="440" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AC.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
